23	 * precision (the maximum number of digits) and scale (the number of digits on right side of dot).
24	 *
25	 * <p>The precision can be up to 38, scale can also be up to 38 (less or equal to precision).
26	 *
27	 * <p>The default precision and scale is (10, 0).
28	 *
29	 * @since 3.0.0
30	 */
31	@Evolving
32	public final class DecimalType extends DataType {
33	  public static final DecimalType USER_DEFAULT = new DecimalType(10, 0);
